⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Peter Wiggin
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Peter Wiggin:C1:88a78f⟧

WHO   — Peter Wiggin — the eldest Wiggin
WHAT  — The Hegemon — the brother left behind on Earth, who turns naked ambition into hard statecraft, conquering not with armies but with words, masks, and an unerring read of every human heart.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Ender Quintet / Ender's Game  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the boy who wanted only to rule learned that ruling is service that costs everything; because cruelty unspent can be forged into order; because the world will tear itself apart unless one cold, clear mind chooses to hold it together — and pays in conscience for the holding.
HOW   — By the pseudonymous voice of Locke and the goading of his sister into the firebrand Demosthenes, by the manipulation of nets and nations, by reading the want and fear in any face and giving it exactly the shape he needs — and, in the end, by the bitter discipline of becoming better than he was born.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I was the brother they were afraid of — so I took the world no one would give me, and I am still learning to deserve it.

